BUILD_ONLY: ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/efe-private:robolab-<images/robolab/VERSION> is never public (docs/protocol/README.md §2.4,
D5). It is kept in the organization's private package as the build cache of the RoboLab tasks: every task's Dockerfile starts
with this recipe (images/robolab/Dockerfile, copied in by scripts/task_conventions.py normalize) and its compose names the
private image in `build.cache_from`. A runner that can pull the image takes its layers; any other runner builds the same
recipe from public sources on its first task (`harbor run` does it; nothing to run by hand).

Why
  The image contains NVIDIA Isaac Sim 5.1 / Omniverse Kit and the Isaac Lab 2.3.2 pip wheels (installed from
  pypi.nvidia.com). NVIDIA licenses them for use, not for redistribution, so the built image may not be published.
  RoboLab itself (github.com/NVlabs/RoboLab v0.3.1, code and its ~6 GB LFS asset library) is Apache-2.0.

What the builder accepts
  - the NVIDIA Isaac Sim / Omniverse license agreement (the recipe sets OMNI_KIT_ACCEPT_EULA=YES and ACCEPT_EULA=Y, and
    every container that runs it accepts it again at launch);
  - NVIDIA's terms for the isaacsim / isaaclab wheels on pypi.nvidia.com;
  - RoboLab's Apache-2.0 licence (its assets are baked in, as RoboLab's own docker/Dockerfile does).
  No account, key or token is needed: everything is downloaded anonymously.

Inputs (all pinned)
  docker.io/nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-base-ubuntu22.04 by digest; Ubuntu packages from snapshot.ubuntu.com at 2026-10-01; uv
  0.13.0 (its image by digest) and the CPython 3.11.17 it installs; RoboLab at commit 9db0aaf (tag v0.3.1) with its git
  LFS assets (every LFS file must arrive); every Python package from images/robolab/uv.lock (`uv sync --frozen`); the
  419 remote files of the asset library from NVIDIA's public Omniverse content bucket, each checked against
  images/robolab/remote_assets.sha256 (mirror_remote_assets.py: the build fails when the bucket serves other bytes, a
  file less or a file more; `--write` re-pins, after a look at the rendering), and the 15 layers that named them pointed
  at the copies under /opt/robolab/assets/_remote. The recipe's three repository files come by URL from this repository
  at a pinned commit that a tag keeps reachable, each checked by its sha256: a change to one of them is a new commit and
  checksum in the recipe and a new VERSION.

Data
  None beyond the image: nothing is mounted or downloaded at run time. The frozen task instances live in the task
  directories.

Host
  Linux x86_64, Docker with BuildKit and the NVIDIA Container Toolkit, an RTX-class NVIDIA GPU with a driver Isaac Sim
  5.1 supports (Isaac renders with RTX even headless; PhysX runs on the CPU). Checked on RTX 4090 and RTX PRO 6000.
  Build: ~60 GB of free disk, network access to github.com (+ its LFS), ghcr.io, snapshot.ubuntu.com, pypi.org,
  pypi.nvidia.com, download.pytorch.org and NVIDIA's Omniverse content bucket
  (omniverse-content-production.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com and its s3-us-west-2 spelling); a cold build takes 20-60 min
  (22 min on a 32-core host). Run: one Isaac simulator per 32 GB of host RAM.

Build and publish (maintainers; from the repository root)
  RCB_PUSH_PRIVATE=1 scripts/build_images.sh builds every image (this one with BuildKit's inline cache); alone:
    docker build --build-arg BUILDKIT_INLINE_CACHE=1 -t ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/efe-private:robolab-$(cat images/robolab/VERSION) images/robolab
    docker push ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/efe-private:robolab-$(cat images/robolab/VERSION)
  A new VERSION: change the tag in the tasks' `cache_from` and normalize them.

Check a build
  The frozen instances must rebuild to their recorded state hashes, and a fresh-process replay of a reference trajectory
  must end in its recorded hash: `harbor run -p tasks/robolab/robolab-banana-in-bowl-i00-privileged -a oracle` (reward 1;
  its verifier replays the trajectory in a fresh process and checks instance_exact). Without network, every mirrored file
  has its pinned hash and no text layer of the library names the bucket by URL:
    docker run --rm --network none ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/efe-private:robolab-$(cat images/robolab/VERSION) sh -c \
      'cd /opt/robolab/assets/_remote && sha256sum -c --quiet /opt/robolab/remote_assets.sha256 && ! grep -rIlE "https?:/+omniverse-content" /opt/robolab/assets --include=*.usda'
